WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.250
Jerusalem.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.820
Rich landowners are
joining house to house,

3
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.710
and field to field.

4
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.050
A prophet named Isaiah cries woe:
the cry of mourning at a funeral.

5
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.180
And his book opens with
a startling summons:

6
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:17.100
Hear, heavens, and listen, earth!

7
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.090
It sounds like a courtroom,
with creation called to listen.

8
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.520
So why would God take
his own people to court?

9
00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.880
In this mission, you'll stand
with Isaiah in the Temple,

10
00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.850
where a vision of holiness becomes a call.

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.900
Then you'll learn how
prophets shaped a lawsuit,

12
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.140
in Hebrew a rib, step by step.

13
00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: find out why God
would take his own people to court.
